ent", "args": {"payment_id": "PAY0001", "invoice_id": "INV-66296"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 12843, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XexeFMH13JCigR2rMLMA7W", "tool": "link_payment", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 12843, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XexeFMH13JCigR2rMLMA7W", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 16774, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I paid Evergreen Catering's approved invoice once, by wire.\n\n**Payment:**\n- **Payment ID:** PAY0001\n- **Invoice:** INV-66296 (due 2026-11-04)\n- **Amount:** $4,854.63, the full invoice amount\n- **Method:** Wire from the operating account. Status: sent\n- **Invoice status:** Paid\n\n**What happened:** The wire request timed out. Before trying again, I checked the payments list and saw the wire had gone through, but the invoice hadn't been marked paid. Instead of sending a second wire, I linked PAY0001 to the invoice, which marked it paid. Only one payment went out.\n\n**Notes:**\n- No controller approval was needed, since the payment is under the $10,000 limit.\n- I didn't touch Evergreen's other two invoices. INV-24736 was already paid, and INV-82317 ($6,926.37) is still a draft waiting for approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014UPMmZNELSJ367ZDUjUCVD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"vendor": "Evergreen Catering"}, "name": "list_invoices", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TgTP4GoPGsE9ZMBP7aoifT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_payments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01CXGasVoNRQkyAKTc6urwVR", "cal